Subject: [PATCH] kbase: never submit JM jobs with dependency sentinel ID zero

The JM ABI ignores pre-dependencies whose atom_id is zero. Submitting the
first vertex/tiler job as atom zero therefore lets the fragment job run
before tiling finishes. Later frames hide the race; synchronous tracing
also hides it. Skip zero both at context startup and on uint8_t wraparound.

--- a/src/panfrost/base/pan_vX_base.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/base/pan_vX_base.c
@@ -1133,7 +1133,10 @@ kbase_submit(kbase k, uint64_t va, unsigned req,
         unsigned slot = (req & PANFROST_JD_REQ_FS) ? 0 : 1;
         unsigned dep_slots[KBASE_SLOT_COUNT];
 
         uint8_t nr = k->atom_number++;
+        /* Atom ID zero means no dependency in the JM ABI. */
+        if (!nr)
+                nr = k->atom_number++;
 
         struct base_jd_atom_v2 atom = {
                 .jc = va,
